fficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c6698986-949b-5e23-a1b3-d50a3d4acb65"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6698986-949b-5e23-a1b3-d50a3d4acb65" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6698986-949b-5e23-a1b3-d50a3d4acb65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f456c94d-ebd4-5f0b-b470-ffd45783554a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-66a20978-052e-5ad7-9f1d-9b0b7ee114ce" "answer-f63ab2d4-d54d-595f-9f13-411bad3bf356" "answer-f456c94d-ebd4-5f0b-b470-ffd45783554a" "answer-b2bc00bc-102f-56a7-ae97-c99fdc494631" "answer-ac9207f2-28a9-50c4-93b1-f0bbca2c7354"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66a20978-052e-5ad7-9f1d-9b0b7ee114ce" :answer/id #uuid "66a20978-052e-5ad7-9f1d-9b0b7ee114ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f63ab2d4-d54d-595f-9f13-411bad3bf356" :answer/id #uuid "f63ab2d4-d54d-595f-9f13-411bad3bf356" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f456c94d-ebd4-5f0b-b470-ffd45783554a" :answer/id #uuid "f456c94d-ebd4-5f0b-b470-ffd45783554a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2bc00bc-102f-56a7-ae97-c99fdc494631" :answer/id #uuid "b2bc00bc-102f-56a7-ae97-c99fdc494631" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac9207f2-28a9-50c4-93b1-f0bbca2c7354" :answer/id #uuid "ac9207f2-28a9-50c4-93b1-f0bbca2c7354" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed1378b7-d665-5e7d-b9bb-42ac28cb1db4" :question/id #uuid "ed1378b7-d665-5e7d-b9bb-42ac28cb1db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-216436" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n\n- $x({x}^{2}+x-6)\\le 0$\n- $x\\le 2$\n- $x\\ge 0$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given inequality is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-6 & \\le 0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-2) & \\le 0 \\\\ -3\\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇏\\,(x({x}^{2}+x-6)\\le 0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-1,$ then ${x}^{2}+x-6=-6\\le 0,$ but $x({x}^{2}+x-6)=6≰0.$\n\n- Condition II is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇒\\,(x\\le 2)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEvery solution of ${x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0$ satisfies $x\\le 2.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+x-6\\le 0)\\,⇏\\,(x\\ge 0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-1,$ then ${x}^{2}+x-6=-6\\le 0,$ but $x≱0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-65d6a9dc-fcc4-5ded-8f64-2cbe1ae88d98"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-65d6a9dc-fcc4-5ded-8f64-2cbe1ae88d98" :answer-field/id #uuid "65d6a9dc-fcc4-5ded-8f64-2cbe1ae88d98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-723b0b18-8d2a-573d-8c7a-b060274c4be8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-79d4f89d-2406-5661-97b9-53a4d47d9095" "answer-f4f07888-45ef-54ff-800d-2f443444b95a" "answer-c63ae798-9fea-58a3-a28e-246e0b2e732f" "answer-723b0b18-8d2a-573d-8c7a-b060274c4be8" "answer-f2226bbc-d85c-51dc-b76d-73e6d3a402ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79d4f89d-2406-5661-97b9-53a4d47d9095" :answer/id #uuid "79d4f89d-2406-5661-97b9-53a4d47d9095" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4f07888-45ef-54ff-800d-2f443444b95a" :answer/id #uuid "f4f07888-45ef-54ff-800d-2f443444b95a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c63ae798-9fea-58a3-a28e-246e0b2e732f" :answer/id #uuid "c63ae798-9fea-58a3-a28e-246e0b2e732f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-723b0b18-8d2a-573d-8c7a-b060274c4be8" :answer/id #uuid "723b0b18-8d2a-573d-8c7a-b060274c4be8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2226bbc-d85c-51dc-b76d-73e6d3a402ad" :answer/id #uuid "f2226bbc-d85c-51dc-b76d-73e6d3a402ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4b376045-26da-55cb-becc-db924f8d2dac" :question/id #uuid "4b376045-26da-55cb-becc-db924f8d2dac" :question/math-academy-id "q-172302" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}$ is an odd number\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n\n- $n$ is odd\n- $n$ is a multiple of $3$\n- $n$ is a multiple of $5$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions. \n\n- Condition I is a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇒\\,(\\text{ }n\\text{ is odd})\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSince ${n}^{2}$ is odd, it must also be true that $n$ is odd.\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }3)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=7$ is not a multiple of $3,$ but ${n}^{2}=49$ is an odd number.\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an odd number})\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }5)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=9$ is not a multiple of $5,$ but ${n}^{2}=81$ is an odd number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0fdc134d-ac74-5fab-ae76-84aa43f0b703"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0fdc134d-ac74-5fab-ae76-84aa43f0b703" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fdc134d-ac74-5fab-ae76-84aa43f0b703" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a8debe43-b8b0-55ab-a68f-d6d8ea9b6da7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-acb5c849-cab1-5f29-a8bd-103025ea3634" "answer-a8debe43-b8b0-55ab-a68f-d6d8ea9b6da7" "answer-1c495edd-fe1e-5f10-9062-4276befeff1e" "answer-80a3cd69-f340-5a70-9070-8ac5442c89a9" "answer-16016d71-db47-5c29-a6f2-a697be2b8d66"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acb5c849-cab1-5f29-a8bd-103025ea3634" :answer/id #uuid "acb5c849-cab1-5f29-a8bd-103025ea3634" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8debe43-b8b0-55ab-a68f-d6d8ea9b6da7" :answer/id #uuid "a8debe43-b8b0-55ab-a68f-d6d8ea9b6da7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c495edd-fe1e-5f10-9062-4276befeff1e" :answer/id #uuid "1c495edd-fe1e-5f10-9062-4276befeff1e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80a3cd69-f340-5a70-9070-8ac5442c89a9" :answer/id #uuid "80a3cd69-f340-5a70-9070-8ac5442c89a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16016d71-db47-5c29-a6f2-a697be2b8d66" :answer/id #uuid "16016d71-db47-5c29-a6f2-a697be2b8d66" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-04618c03-3ca0-590d-b082-33d1176f03c4" :question/id #uuid "04618c03-3ca0-590d-b082-33d1176f03c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-172300" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}$ is an even number\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n\n- $n$ is an odd number\n- $n$ is a positive number\n- $n$ is a multiple of $2$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions. \n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number })\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is an odd number})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=2$ is not an odd number but ${2}^{2}$ is an even number.\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇏\\,(\\text{ is a positive number})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=-2$ is not a positive number, but $(-2)^{2}$ is an even number.\n\n- Condition III is a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇒\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }2)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSince ${n}^{2}$ is even, it must also be true that $n$ is even. Therefore, $n$ is a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53166bf7-c886-5b0e-983e-f872f31bc094"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53166bf7-c886-5b0e-983e-f872f31bc094" :answer-field/id #uuid "53166bf7-c886-5b0e-983e-f872f31bc094" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a3107ee-9464-55c3-b2c0-aa35b357416e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-782a27b8-b034-5c8a-9112-6b1dee6f9a88" "answer-0fdd5fd1-d207-54b2-b6ad-11c0a56f64d5" "answer-ff258869-ea00-57cc-90ca-d8880f812d1b" "answer-5a3107ee-9464-55c3-b2c0-aa35b357416e" "answer-60328983-7337-550c-99ac-442094612dcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-782a27b8-b034-5c8a-9112-6b1dee6f9a88" :answer/id #uuid "782a27b8-b034-5c8a-9112-6b1dee6f9a88" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fdd5fd1-d207-54b2-b6ad-11c0a56f64d5" :answer/id #uuid "0fdd5fd1-d207-54b2-b6ad-11c0a56f64d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff258869-ea00-57cc-90ca-d8880f812d1b" :answer/id #uuid "ff258869-ea00-57cc-90ca-d8880f812d1b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a3107ee-9464-55c3-b2c0-aa35b357416e" :answer/id #uuid "5a3107ee-9464-55c3-b2c0-aa35b357416e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60328983-7337-550c-99ac-442094612dcf" :answer/id #uuid "60328983-7337-550c-99ac-442094612dcf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5ef2cacc-c405-55b2-8430-66b58129ad71" :question/id #uuid "5ef2cacc-c405-55b2-8430-66b58129ad71" :question/math-academy-id "q-172298" :question/problem "$\\,$ $|x-2|=6$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n\n- $x>4$\n- $|x|<10$\n- $x=8$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x-2| & =6 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 6 \\\\ x & =-4,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇏\\,(x>4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then $|x-2|=6,$ but $x≯4.$\n\n- Condition II is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇒\\,(|x|<10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEach solution of $|x-2|=6$ satisfies $|x|<10.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(|x-2|=6)\\,⇏\\,(x=8)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then $|x-2|=6,$ but $x\\ne 8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3dddff4c-3d97-5829-a5f6-3f51ccd09496"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3dddff4c-3d97-5829-a5f6-3f51ccd09496" :answer-field/id #uuid "3dddff4c-3d97-5829-a5f6-3f51ccd09496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-266cebd5-1df8-59d8-9d7f-5e97061db023" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14e7d224-a6a4-59f8-8fdd-0ff468f330c1" "answer-ae91a6ae-e621-5467-9306-e9dd3d875c36" "answer-f3cd468a-9cc8-5dc8-8fd8-8420399559dc" "answer-266cebd5-1df8-59d8-9d7f-5e97061db023" "answer-49f2aae6-e3f9-535f-82d1-b68b36c62b4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14e7d224-a6a4-59f8-8fdd-0ff468f330c1" :answer/id #uuid "14e7d224-a6a4-59f8-8fdd-0ff468f330c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae91a6ae-e621-5467-9306-e9dd3d875c36" :answer/id #uuid "ae91a6ae-e621-5467-9306-e9dd3d875c36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3cd468a-9cc8-5dc8-8fd8-8420399559dc" :answer/id #uuid "f3cd468a-9cc8-5dc8-8fd8-8420399559dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-266cebd5-1df8-59d8-9d7f-5e97061db023" :answer/id #uuid "266cebd5-1df8-59d8-9d7f-5e97061db023" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49f2aae6-e3f9-535f-82d1-b68b36c62b4b" :answer/id #uuid "49f2aae6-e3f9-535f-82d1-b68b36c62b4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152453 :question/problem "$\\,$ ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n\n- $x=1$\n- $x<0$\n- $|x|<5$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-3 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇏\\,(x=1)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-3,$ then ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0,$ but $x\\ne 1.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇏\\,(x<0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=1,$ then ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0,$ but $x≮0.$\n\n- Condition III is a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-3=0)\\,⇒\\,(|x|<5)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nEach solution of ${x}^{2}+2x-3=0$ satisfies $|x|<5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149249 :answer-field/correct 17592186149250 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-10fd92b2-5e05-5850-b7d2-d8140b9fd04f" :question/id #uuid "10fd92b2-5e05-5850-b7d2-d8140b9fd04f" :question/math-academy-id "q-172315" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}=16$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\n- $n=4$\n- $-4<n<4$\n- $|n|<16$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}=16)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ (n+4)(n-4) & =0 \\\\ n & =-4,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=4)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=4,$ then ${n}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(-4<n<4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2} & =(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =1\\ne 16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|<16)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then $|n|<16,$ but ${n}^{2}=1\\ne 16.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5fa13c5f-22a6-5392-8f0c-0c5ab3fb743c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5fa13c5f-22a6-5392-8f0c-0c5ab3fb743c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fa13c5f-22a6-5392-8f0c-0c5ab3fb743c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-09e65e4f-7780-5d04-b434-5b982a0cc738" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45df796e-175e-502d-b952-1965fb870644" "answer-09e65e4f-7780-5d04-b434-5b982a0cc738" "answer-f6b29929-e1a6-5202-b99e-176a6e1f7c4c" "answer-f1ad22a1-7d29-515b-8d15-5657d1156609" "answer-8108a9c5-ed15-5e27-beb5-e7a64c2d63e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45df796e-175e-502d-b952-1965fb870644" :answer/id #uuid "45df796e-175e-502d-b952-1965fb870644" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09e65e4f-7780-5d04-b434-5b982a0cc738" :answer/id #uuid "09e65e4f-7780-5d04-b434-5b982a0cc738" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6b29929-e1a6-5202-b99e-176a6e1f7c4c" :answer/id #uuid "f6b29929-e1a6-5202-b99e-176a6e1f7c4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1ad22a1-7d29-515b-8d15-5657d1156609" :answer/id #uuid "f1ad22a1-7d29-515b-8d15-5657d1156609" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8108a9c5-ed15-5e27-beb5-e7a64c2d63e1" :answer/id #uuid "8108a9c5-ed15-5e27-beb5-e7a64c2d63e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-28567992-ba7f-5623-ad07-13abe4be416c" :question/id #uuid "28567992-ba7f-5623-ad07-13abe4be416c" :question/math-academy-id "q-172325" :question/problem "$\\,$ $x+1>4$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\n- $|x|>3$\n- $x>3$\n- $x>4$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & >4 \\\\ x & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|x|>3)\\,⇏\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then we have $x+1=-3≯4.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(x>3)\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $x>3,$ then $x+1>4.$\n\n- Condition III is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(x>4)\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $x>4,$ then  $x+1>5>4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0f2ced5e-9852-5fb0-9bab-d51b27fc2767"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0f2ced5e-9852-5fb0-9bab-d51b27fc2767" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2ced5e-9852-5fb0-9bab-d51b27fc2767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c2efefc8-22d0-53d7-a45f-92c16998fbf2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c263e106-7fef-58ab-9b12-f17370ec03a5" "answer-c2efefc8-22d0-53d7-a45f-92c16998fbf2" "answer-0141819d-fce9-5dfe-8363-7f37fca55fde" "answer-f0f792f1-74bf-5213-8686-058d2f686f27" "answer-372fbdd1-3e8c-57d3-b2f8-c9c3f7462ad6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c263e106-7fef-58ab-9b12-f17370ec03a5" :answer/id #uuid "c263e106-7fef-58ab-9b12-f17370ec03a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2efefc8-22d0-53d7-a45f-92c16998fbf2" :answer/id #uuid "c2efefc8-22d0-53d7-a45f-92c16998fbf2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0141819d-fce9-5dfe-8363-7f37fca55fde" :answer/id #uuid "0141819d-fce9-5dfe-8363-7f37fca55fde" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0f792f1-74bf-5213-8686-058d2f686f27" :answer/id #uuid "f0f792f1-74bf-5213-8686-058d2f686f27" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-372fbdd1-3e8c-57d3-b2f8-c9c3f7462ad6" :answer/id #uuid "372fbdd1-3e8c-57d3-b2f8-c9c3f7462ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152455 :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}+2n-3=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\n- $n=1$\n- $n<0$\n- $|n|<5$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2n-3 & =0 \\\\ (n+3)(n-1) & =0 \\\\ n & =-3,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=1)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=1,$ then ${n}^{2}+2n-3=0.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n<0)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2n-3 & =(-1)^{2}+2(-1)-3 \\\\  & =1-2-3 \\\\  & =-4 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|<5)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+2n-3=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then $|n|<5,$ but ${n}^{2}+2n-3\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149261 :answer-field/correct 17592186149262 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-e4cdd56d-10e6-5abf-be98-585e1ce87428" :question/id #uuid "e4cdd56d-10e6-5abf-be98-585e1ce87428" :question/math-academy-id "q-172322" :question/problem "$\\,$ $a\\ge 10$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\n- $a=10$\n- $a>15$\n- $a>5$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a=10)\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $a=10,$ then $a\\ge 10.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a>15)\\,⇒\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $a>15,$ then $a\\ge 10.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(a>5)\\,⇏\\,(a\\ge 10)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $a=7,$ then we have $a≱10.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ecfcee5e-24eb-56dc-ac84-c2b7a4109c97"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ecfcee5e-24eb-56dc-ac84-c2b7a4109c97" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecfcee5e-24eb-56dc-ac84-c2b7a4109c97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a2f79458-4c2b-54d4-87ba-d97c53f760aa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2f79458-4c2b-54d4-87ba-d97c53f760aa" "answer-a41ae0db-cfac-58d5-a3cd-32a56a56b7c5" "answer-e3ec35dc-2bc0-5873-a893-a0c100b00486" "answer-fec036cb-7688-5ab9-89fc-cd9daabe9e4f" "answer-b877dce5-c49c-5f58-9963-36f0cb4433cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2f79458-4c2b-54d4-87ba-d97c53f760aa" :answer/id #uuid "a2f79458-4c2b-54d4-87ba-d97c53f760aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a41ae0db-cfac-58d5-a3cd-32a56a56b7c5" :answer/id #uuid "a41ae0db-cfac-58d5-a3cd-32a56a56b7c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3ec35dc-2bc0-5873-a893-a0c100b00486" :answer/id #uuid "e3ec35dc-2bc0-5873-a893-a0c100b00486" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fec036cb-7688-5ab9-89fc-cd9daabe9e4f" :answer/id #uuid "fec036cb-7688-5ab9-89fc-cd9daabe9e4f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b877dce5-c49c-5f58-9963-36f0cb4433cb" :answer/id #uuid "b877dce5-c49c-5f58-9963-36f0cb4433cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-00b6d002-6ca8-5b5f-a710-55bc4f02fb94" :question/id #uuid "00b6d002-6ca8-5b5f-a710-55bc4f02fb94" :question/math-academy-id "q-216443" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}+7n+12=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\n- $n\\ge -4$\n- $n=-4$\n- $|n|\\le 4$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\n$$\n\nNote that the solutions to the given equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+7n+12 & =0 \\\\ (n+4)(n+3) & =0 \\\\ n & =-4,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n\\ge -4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=0,$ then $n\\ge -4,$ but ${n}^{2}+7n+12\\ne 0.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=-4)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=-4,$ then ${n}^{2}+7n+12=0.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|\\le 4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=0,$ then $|n|\\le 4,$ but ${n}^{2}+7n+12\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4355a00e-8da5-5b0a-966f-b3794b720dfc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4355a00e-8da5-5b0a-966f-b3794b720dfc" :answer-field/id #uuid "4355a00e-8da5-5b0a-966f-b3794b720dfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8a983d6-5780-5e7e-be56-356425ae752f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4cbca457-7b68-56e6-9d5d-1f73524010a6" "answer-844f10e3-5ed7-5640-92ef-91197a14bf26" "answer-045755e2-d591-54ee-8420-3178cdc956ba" "answer-f8a983d6-5780-5e7e-be56-356425ae752f" "answer-72cbce88-fa64-5e61-8cc8-f4a2aeb564ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4cbca457-7b68-56e6-9d5d-1f73524010a6" :answer/id #uuid "4cbca457-7b68-56e6-9d5d-1f73524010a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-844f10e3-5ed7-5640-92ef-91197a14bf26" :answer/id #uuid "844f10e3-5ed7-5640-92ef-91197a14bf26" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-045755e2-d591-54ee-8420-3178cdc956ba" :answer/id #uuid "045755e2-d591-54ee-8420-3178cdc956ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8a983d6-5780-5e7e-be56-356425ae752f" :answer/id #uuid "f8a983d6-5780-5e7e-be56-356425ae752f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72cbce88-fa64-5e61-8cc8-f4a2aeb564ed" :answer/id #uuid "72cbce88-fa64-5e61-8cc8-f4a2aeb564ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9dd0c0c2-7652-5690-ae78-53d067f574fa" :question/id #uuid "9dd0c0c2-7652-5690-ae78-53d067f574fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-183485" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(x)=2$\n- $f(x)={x}^{2}+C,$ for any $C\\in R$\n- $f(x)={x}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int 2x\\,dx \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C\\in R$ is the arbitrary constant.\n\nMoreover, the differential equation ${f}^{″}(x)=2$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\int 2\\,dx \\\\  & =2x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D\\in R$ is another arbitrary constant.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇍\\,({f}^{″}(x)=2)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+x,$ we have ${f}^{′}(x)=2x+1,$ and so the statement ${f}^{″}(x)=2$  is true but ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne 2x.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: The statement ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is true *if and only if* $f(x)={x}^{2}+C,$ for any $C\\in R.$\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇒\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇐\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇔\\,(f(x)={x}^{2}+C)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)=2x)\\,⇏\\,(f(x)={x}^{2})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)={x}^{2}+1$ the statement ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ is true but $f(x)\\ne {x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dae23ffb-af9a-509a-99d1-3643141889bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dae23ffb-af9a-509a-99d1-3643141889bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "dae23ffb-af9a-509a-99d1-3643141889bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8bc9b04f-28fc-5724-95bd-6fe1adf8f451" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b2e878cb-1ec8-5097-aa5d-f6e3f76faa62" "answer-2a5084f6-69e4-520c-a5e4-b275a8c4693a" "answer-67b27e1c-7265-5812-b062-c84b86be6606" "answer-8bc9b04f-28fc-5724-95bd-6fe1adf8f451" "answer-48cc24d8-8ada-5963-8ea2-3d096ef3b9be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2e878cb-1ec8-5097-aa5d-f6e3f76faa62" :answer/id #uuid "b2e878cb-1ec8-5097-aa5d-f6e3f76faa62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a5084f6-69e4-520c-a5e4-b275a8c4693a" :answer/id #uuid "2a5084f6-69e4-520c-a5e4-b275a8c4693a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67b27e1c-7265-5812-b062-c84b86be6606" :answer/id #uuid "67b27e1c-7265-5812-b062-c84b86be6606" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8bc9b04f-28fc-5724-95bd-6fe1adf8f451" :answer/id #uuid "8bc9b04f-28fc-5724-95bd-6fe1adf8f451" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48cc24d8-8ada-5963-8ea2-3d096ef3b9be" :answer/id #uuid "48cc24d8-8ada-5963-8ea2-3d096ef3b9be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5904ff03-6479-54c0-a38b-31e73684000e" :question/id #uuid "5904ff03-6479-54c0-a38b-31e73684000e" :question/math-academy-id "q-216449" :question/problem "$\\,$ $12∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n\n- $2∣x$ and $6∣x$\n- $3∣x$ and $4∣x$\n- $3∣x$ and $8∣x$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇍\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }6∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=6$ is divisible by $2$ and by $6$ but not divisible by $12.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $12$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $3$ and $4.$\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇒\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇐\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇔\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }4∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(12∣x)\\,⇏\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }8∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=12$ is divisible by $12$ but not divisible by $8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-be0157e5-7ad5-51d5-b39b-5c2649601c3b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-be0157e5-7ad5-51d5-b39b-5c2649601c3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "be0157e5-7ad5-51d5-b39b-5c2649601c3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f78301a0-d9e6-54f9-81a3-411506bab620" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78c0055c-c885-59cb-a2a0-5eac59047ead" "answer-06e8bf70-2a60-5941-87e1-f5189ba873f4" "answer-5970156a-402e-53cd-9465-784a6bc663ad" "answer-f78301a0-d9e6-54f9-81a3-411506bab620" "answer-c3a7bdcd-3396-5c6e-a601-a161e66d71fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78c0055c-c885-59cb-a2a0-5eac59047ead" :answer/id #uuid "78c0055c-c885-59cb-a2a0-5eac59047ead" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06e8bf70-2a60-5941-87e1-f5189ba873f4" :answer/id #uuid "06e8bf70-2a60-5941-87e1-f5189ba873f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5970156a-402e-53cd-9465-784a6bc663ad" :answer/id #uuid "5970156a-402e-53cd-9465-784a6bc663ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f78301a0-d9e6-54f9-81a3-411506bab620" :answer/id #uuid "f78301a0-d9e6-54f9-81a3-411506bab620" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3a7bdcd-3396-5c6e-a601-a161e66d71fb" :answer/id #uuid "c3a7bdcd-3396-5c6e-a601-a161e66d71fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f653d451-6beb-59b1-affd-6d539e9553ca" :question/id #uuid "f653d451-6beb-59b1-affd-6d539e9553ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-216447" :question/problem "$\\,$ $18∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n\n- $2∣x$ and $9∣x$\n- $3∣x$ and $6∣x$\n- $72∣x$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $18$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $2$ and $9.$\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇒\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇐\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇔\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }9∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇍\\,(3∣x\\text{ and }6∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=6$ is divisible by $3$ and by $6$ but not divisible by $18.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(18∣x)\\,⇏\\,(72∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=18$ is divisible by $18$ but not divisible by $72.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2cdfba46-cdcd-52d6-a6f1-f3d15b8a74a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2cdfba46-cdcd-52d6-a6f1-f3d15b8a74a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cdfba46-cdcd-52d6-a6f1-f3d15b8a74a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf6d3a5f-e04d-5107-9d35-a0710f0ab915" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7ffe0ac0-8a5a-58ee-a4f9-48dcb58891b0" "answer-cf6d3a5f-e04d-5107-9d35-a0710f0ab915" "answer-0ca9ed22-18ac-5eeb-9f53-e13bcad40e04" "answer-2b1c1196-eb9d-51a7-8da8-862fff9a154f" "answer-81e54969-5398-5218-be00-7fbc3b23054c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ffe0ac0-8a5a-58ee-a4f9-48dcb58891b0" :answer/id #uuid "7ffe0ac0-8a5a-58ee-a4f9-48dcb58891b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf6d3a5f-e04d-5107-9d35-a0710f0ab915" :answer/id #uuid "cf6d3a5f-e04d-5107-9d35-a0710f0ab915" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ca9ed22-18ac-5eeb-9f53-e13bcad40e04" :answer/id #uuid "0ca9ed22-18ac-5eeb-9f53-e13bcad40e04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b1c1196-eb9d-51a7-8da8-862fff9a154f" :answer/id #uuid "2b1c1196-eb9d-51a7-8da8-862fff9a154f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81e54969-5398-5218-be00-7fbc3b23054c" :answer/id #uuid "81e54969-5398-5218-be00-7fbc3b23054c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e1662ac-5299-5cc7-92ca-68567f121fc8" :question/id #uuid "8e1662ac-5299-5cc7-92ca-68567f121fc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-183429" :question/problem "$\\,$ $20∣x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n\n- $2∣x$ and $10∣x$\n- $4∣x$ and $5∣x$\n- $100∣x$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇍\\,(2∣x\\text{ and }10∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=10$ is divisible by $2$ and by $10$ but not divisible by $20.$\n\n- Condition II is both necessary and sufficient: A number is divisible by $20$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $4$ and $5.$\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇒\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇐\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇔\\,(4∣x\\text{ and }5∣x)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n(20∣x)\\,⇏\\,(100∣x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $x=20$ is divisible by $20$ but not divisible by $100.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9d8a18c8-c94d-53a1-9598-3f56ab83bdc6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d8a18c8-c94d-53a1-9598-3f56ab83bdc6" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d8a18c8-c94d-53a1-9598-3f56ab83bdc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-41c86782-467c-5503-8573-af98661637c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-686fb17a-2611-5f1c-bdba-c5c19a1d121a" "answer-83a71146-83dd-5de6-95b8-b27059ff5408" "answer-bba394c5-1fc5-5d3a-b4f9-867f1cffef57" "answer-41c86782-467c-5503-8573-af98661637c4" "answer-3ce83eb5-512d-54ec-a688-0337fd49e4a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-686fb17a-2611-5f1c-bdba-c5c19a1d121a" :answer/id #uuid "686fb17a-2611-5f1c-bdba-c5c19a1d121a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83a71146-83dd-5de6-95b8-b27059ff5408" :answer/id #uuid "83a71146-83dd-5de6-95b8-b27059ff5408" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bba394c5-1fc5-5d3a-b4f9-867f1cffef57" :answer/id #uuid "bba394c5-1fc5-5d3a-b4f9-867f1cffef57" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41c86782-467c-5503-8573-af98661637c4" :answer/id #uuid "41c86782-467c-5503-8573-af98661637c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ce83eb5-512d-54ec-a688-0337fd49e4a0" :answer/id #uuid "3ce83eb5-512d-54ec-a688-0337fd49e4a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-390cc44c-87e5-5905-81de-8b4495a342fd" :question/id #uuid "390cc44c-87e5-5905-81de-8b4495a342fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-216459" :question/problem "$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n\n- $f$ is a differentiable function\n- $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$\n- $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C,$ for any $C\\in R$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C\\in R$ is the arbitrary constant.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇍\\,(f\\text{ is a differentiable function})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the function $f(x)={e}^{x}$ is a differentiable function but ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne {sec}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇏\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1,$ the statement ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is true but $f(x)\\ne \\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1.$\n\n- Condition III is both necessary and sufficient: The statement ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is true *if and only if* $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C,$ for any $C\\in R.$\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇒\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇐\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇔\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-380b7b8c-81dc-5fe3-b1fa-945984d0fd5b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-380b7b8c-81dc-5fe3-b1fa-945984d0fd5b" :answer-field/id #uuid "380b7b8c-81dc-5fe3-b1fa-945984d0fd5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ad66aa9-02b1-539d-9ed6-634cc266d1f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aa91d31c-1b7c-51c5-bbcc-d92d41570034" "answer-1e6db338-0cb7-51e2-ac01-95935810d0ee" "answer-4a289173-5b61-589f-ba66-f52456ff017e" "answer-3ffe5c1b-c4bb-59cc-9a1d-6ddf172d759f" "answer-9ad66aa9-02b1-539d-9ed6-634cc266d1f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa91d31c-1b7c-51c5-bbcc-d92d41570034" :answer/id #uuid "aa91d31c-1b7c-51c5-bbcc-d92d41570034" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e6db338-0cb7-51e2-ac01-95935810d0ee" :answer/id #uuid "1e6db338-0cb7-51e2-ac01-95935810d0ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a289173-5b61-589f-ba66-f52456ff017e" :answer/id #uuid "4a289173-5b61-589f-ba66-f52456ff017e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ffe5c1b-c4bb-59cc-9a1d-6ddf172d759f" :answer/id #uuid "3ffe5c1b-c4bb-59cc-9a1d-6ddf172d759f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ad66aa9-02b1-539d-9ed6-634cc266d1f2" :answer/id #uuid "9ad66aa9-02b1-539d-9ed6-634cc266d1f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153432 :tutorial/content "Consider the truth table for $S \\Rightarrow N$ below. Note that the implication is true $({\\color{blue}\\textrm{T}})$ in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th rows. \n\n| $S$ | $N$ | $S \\Rightarrow N$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}\\textrm T$ | $\\color{red}\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue}\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue}\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue}\\textrm T$ |\n\nOf the three rows where the implication is true, $S$ is true $({\\color{red}\\textrm{T}})$ only in the $1$st row, and $N$ is also true $({\\color{red}\\textrm{T}})$ in this row. \n\nSo, if the implication is true, $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is called a **sufficient condition** for $N.$\n\nOn the other hand, if $S$ is true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is also true. Therefore, $N$ is called a **necessary condition** for $S.$ \nHowever, $N$ being true *does not guarantee* that $S$ is true, as we can see from the $3$rd row in the truth table.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textbf{S}\\textrm{ufficient} \\: \\Rightarrow \\: \\textbf{N}\\textrm{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nLet's look at some examples:\n\n- Consider the following true implication:\n\n$$\na > 0\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad a^2 > 0\n$$\n\nWe can label each part of the statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\big( \\, a > 0 \\, \\big)}_{\\large\\textrm{sufficient}} \n\\: \\Rightarrow \\: \n\\underbrace{\\big( \\, a^2 > 0 \\, \\big)}_{\\large\\textrm{necessary}}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- $a > 0$ is a *sufficient* condition for $a^2 > 0.$  In other words, $a > 0$ *guarantees* that $a^2 > 0.$\n\n- $a^2 > 0$ is a *necessary* condition for $a > 0.$ In other words, if $a > 0,$ it is necessary that $a^2 > 0.$ However, $a^2 > 0$ *does not guarantee* that $a > 0.$\n\n- Suppose your teacher promises that *if* you score at least $90$ on the exam, *then* you will receive an $A.$ We can express this promise as the following implication:\n![](images/1b/1b2bcf888775f0be1dfc6d7b85c546c2f4c535bc0f04a7dadaceb06a0ab8110a.svg)\nLet's assume the teacher is telling the truth, so the implication is true. We can label each part of our implication as follows:\n![](images/5b/5b0dccacbb0c14d3b7c9a7a69f1cddda6b3a464bb2ae86b95989798d931d71d3.svg)\nTherefore:\n\n- Scoring at least $90$ on the exam is a *sufficient* condition for getting an $A.$ In other words, scoring at least $90$ *guarantees* that you'll get an $A.$\n\n- Getting an $A$ is a *necessary* condition for scoring at least $90.$ In other words, if you score at least $90,$ it necessarily follows that you'll receive $A.$ \n\nHowever, getting an $A$ *does not guarantee* that you scored at least $90$ on the exam. For example, the teacher may have decided to award an $A$ despite a score smaller than 90 if the exam was particularly tough that year." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153444 :tutorial/content "Suppose that an equivalence $P \\Leftrightarrow Q$ is true. Then, we have the following terminology:\n\n- $P$ is a **necessary and sufficient condition** for $Q$\n\n- $Q$ is a **necessary and sufficient condition** for $P$\n\nFor example, consider the following two predicates:\n\n- $35 \\mid n$\n\n- $5 \\mid n$ and $7 \\mid n$\n\nThese are both necessary and sufficient conditions for each other. \n\nIndeed, recall that a number is divisible by $35$ *if and only if* it's divisible by both $5$ and $7.$ In other words, we have\n\n![](images/f8/f850149a190068a3acc1225f6d56a73faef368e45ef69c1878eb933f94bc2f2b.svg)\n\nand\n\n![](images/7e/7eddbd9e552b236b3beca479b9f1e1d702709797dd087fe5d365af5ddac19ef2.svg)\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n![](images/e6/e6d8d5fa95eee18645f6c7fed335d31cc4816900b91cb8697662b5cdf106b0ba.svg)\n\nIn words:\n\n- $\\big( 35 \\mid n \\big)$ *is necessary and sufficient for* ![](images/de/de6cda8624f7ab07fab89d309b47cd0b8908aa5c04a9f5cb142add5f2403ab6a.svg)\n\n- ![](images/0e/0e2189b2579fb028fb41d1eeb58494cdb591315f6b0ac0bae72ed848479b879a.svg) *is necessary and sufficient for* $\\big( 35 \\mid n \\big).$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152377 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
